      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Event loop lag p99",
      "description": "How long a task waits before the Node.js event loop runs it, at the 99th percentile. Under load this should stay in the low milliseconds. Sustained lag above 100ms means the single Node.js thread is saturated and the UI, webhooks and triggers are all being delayed together; above 500ms n8n is effectively unresponsive.",
